_footprints:
Four different footprints, deliberately unrelated:
  visual   - the image, which may cover half the screen and is nobody's business but the renderer's;
  logical  - "footprint": the cells the thing occupies in the world model, usually one;
  collision- NOT here. Scenery never collides. A redwood that blocks movement blocks it because the MAP puts a solid tile on its anchor cell, and "requires_solid" makes the validator prove it. Simulation stays in the grid;
  occlusion- "occluder": the polygon that blocks light, same schema as a tile's, at most the logical footprint.
